// The standard types, by name: ty_std (signedness.id) reads one cell of stdty. An earlier version had one
// function per cell (ty_long, ty_ulong, ty_charp), because a single ty_std(i) would have made every call site
// carry a magic number. They are named now: the call sites pass std_long, std_ulong or std_charp from
// conf.id, so the number has one place and a name, and the per-cell functions were literal-only
// duplicates of one another (E0407). Cell 1 (unsigned int) is read inline by num_uty: a function reading it
// matches idstd's idstd_ec_t_extra.
